      },
      "lineNbr": 696,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-10T09:50:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e For clarification, VirtualMachineConfig.isCompatibleWith is not only for just checking difference of VirtualMachineConfig, but also for keeping VM identity \n\nYeah. If we think changing some config value should change the identity, it should cause isCompatibleWith to return false (so the VM owner can tell), but we should also make sure it really does change the identity.\n\nHow exactly the identity is computed is changing - it used to be pure DICE, but we use Secretkeeper if possible. Either way we want a VM using network to have a different DICE chain; either explicitly visible, or encoded in the hidden input to one of the DICE nodes. Ideally in a backward compatible way, so existing no-network VMs retain their secrets over OS update.\n\nYou should talk to @shikhapanwar@google.com about this. (We should document it somewhere too.)",
      "parentUuid": "eca28222_5186fc5d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 696,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 696,
        "endChar": 99
      },
      "revId": "9386bbbcc0e338a4cad339a90e60ab30a9304b39",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
