      "writtenOn": "2024-06-06T10:35:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we don\u0027t allow a protected VM to use network, shouldn\u0027t we report that when you call VirtualMachineConfig.Builder.build(), rather than wait until they try to start it? That would be a much friendlier experience.\n\nAlso: UnsupportedOperationException doesn\u0027t seem like the right exception, if we do throw it here. Where does it come from? I\u0027d expect it to be wrapped in a VirtualMachineException.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2338,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2347,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "9386bbbcc0e338a4cad339a90e60ab30a9304b39",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6e2756c4_e8cfe7e3",
        "filename": "tests/testapk/src/java/com/android/microdroid/test/MicrodroidTests.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 2347,
      "author": {
        "id": 1950816
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-10T01:54:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In our previous discussions, I understood supporting network for non-pVM is required for ferrochrome so urgent, but not for pVMs. So that\u0027s why I\u0027ve defined the exception as unsupported operation.\n\nI also considered reporting it from the Java side, but it\u0027ll need guards in 2 distinguished places. But I\u0027m still not sure if introducing more \u0027interim\u0027 guards for friendlier experience is good.\n\n\u003e Where does it come from?\n\nFrom `create_vm_internal` in virtmgr. I thought here\u0027s the right place to handle all requests.\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/virtualizationmanager/src/aidl.rs;l\u003d609-626",
      "parentUuid": "f01591b7_f8cf8222",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2338,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2347,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "9386bbbcc0e338a4cad339a90e60ab30a9304b39",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fb09d965_b63e7791",
        "filename": "tests/testapk/src/java/com/android/microdroid/test/MicrodroidTests.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 2347,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-06-10T09:50:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t throw UnsupportedOperationException anywhere else, I think. We wrap almost everything in VirtualMachineException. And we don\u0027t seem to be documenting the restriction, nor the exception, anywhere.\n\nI would really prefer to check it in `VirtualMachineConfig.Builder.build()`; that\u0027s where we currently enforce all the other rules about incompatible sets of config options, and we can give a clear error message (and add a simple test). And if you do that, the throw from `create_vm_internal` becomes unreachable, so you don\u0027t have to do any work to handle it.",
      "parentUuid": "6e2756c4_e8cfe7e3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2338,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2347,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "9386bbbcc0e338a4cad339a90e60ab30a9304b39",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
