      "writtenOn": "2024-06-11T04:19:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Sorry, I am not sure I am following this patch. If the only use case for networking is Ferrochrome, why do we expose this functionality to Microdroid?\n\nIn my understanding, Microdroid is a reference VM type in AVF. And network feature is the common feature for all type of VMs. That\u0027s why I put this into `VirtualMachineConfig`. However, I agree that there may be no future use cases around Microdroid with network feature. In this case, should I move this into `VirtualMachineCustomImageConfig`?\n\n\u003e I would really prefer to check it in VirtualMachineConfig.Builder.build()\n\nAcknowledged, I\u0027ll handle it from Java API side as well. But paused for a moment to get a clear answer of above question.",
      "parentUuid": "7d4cfbf8_71f1134f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2338,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2347,
        "endChar": 5
      },
